{"format":"telly-addicts-eps","v":1,"show":"Blind Date","i":8077,"eps":[{"s":1,"e":1,"t":"Series 1, Show 1","a":"1985-11-30","l":60,"d":"Debbie from Southport chooses between three very different guys, and a single guy with an eight-inch beard chooses from three feisty girls. Paul and Caroline are set up on a blind date in romantic Paris, while Amanda and Airz are sent off to Barcelona."},{"s":1,"e":2,"t":"Series 1, Show 2","a":"1985-12-07","l":60},{"s":1,"e":3,"t":"Series 1, Show 3","a":"1985-12-14","l":60},{"s":1,"e":4,"t":"Series 1, Show 4","a":"1985-12-21","l":60},{"s":1,"e":5,"t":"Series 1, Show 5","a":"1985-12-28","l":60},{"s":1,"e":6,"t":"Series 1, Show 6","a":"1986-01-04","l":60},{"s":1,"e":7,"t":"Series 1, Show 7","a":"1986-01-11","l":60},{"s":2,"e":1,"t":"Series 2, Show 1","a":"1986-08-30","l":60,"d":"One lucky single chooses from three suitors by personality alone. Singles bring their dogs along for the first time in the hopes of getting some puppy love, and self-titled 'diva' Devorshka chooses between a plumber, a banker and an accountant."},{"s":2,"e":2,"t":"Series 2, Show 2","a":"1986-09-06","l":60,"d":"A dashing digger driver gets his pick of the single girls, and a drama teacher is looking for her leading man. Plus, did Devorshka and Larry find love in Ayia Napa, and was pug-loving Ollie and Lauren's date in Brighton hot dog or dogmeat?"},{"s":2,"e":3,"t":"Series 2, Show 3","a":"1986-09-13","l":60,"d":"Ant is looking for an older woman with experience, good looks and a lust for life."},{"s":2,"e":4,"t":"Series 2, Show 4","a":"1986-09-20","l":60,"d":"A dental manager from Eastbourne chooses between a picture framer, a health care worker and a sausage maker. Plus Paul reveals big news about Rosie and Conor - things didn't quite go to plan, leading to what must be a first for 'Blind Date'."},{"s":2,"e":5,"t":"Series 2, Show 5","a":"1986-09-27","l":60,"d":"Reformed bad boy Tyrell is looking to settle down, but which girl will steal his heart? Then it's all about the boys as nightclub host Joni is looking for his dream man."},{"s":2,"e":6,"t":"Series 2, Show 6","a":"1986-10-04","l":60,"d":"A white witch from Preston is looking to cast a spell over three eligible bachelors. Ex-military man Dean from Wiltshire is on the hunt for his dream girl."},{"s":2,"e":7,"t":"Series 2, Show 7","a":"1986-10-11","l":60},{"s":2,"e":8,"t":"Series 2, Show 8","a":"1986-10-18","l":60},{"s":2,"e":9,"t":"Series 2, Show 9","a":"1986-10-25","l":60},{"s":2,"e":10,"t":"Series 2, Show 10","a":"1986-11-01","l":60},{"s":2,"e":11,"t":"Series 2, Show 11","a":"1986-11-08","l":60},{"s":2,"e":12,"t":"Series 2, Show 12","a":"1986-11-15","l":60},{"s":2,"e":13,"t":"Series 2, Show 13","a":"1986-11-22","l":60},{"s":2,"e":14,"t":"Series 2, Show 14","a":"1986-11-29","l":60},{"s":2,"e":15,"t":"Series 2, Show 15","a":"1986-12-21","l":60},{"s":3,"e":1,"t":"Series 3, Show 1","a":"1987-09-05","l":60,"d":"Geordie girl Cali gets to choose from three muscled hunks. Single Irish mummy's boy Barry brings his mother Anne to the studio to help him choose his date, which proves to be a shock to the three single girls hoping to be picked."},{"s":3,"e":2,"t":"Series 3, Show 2","a":"1987-09-12","l":60,"d":"A single mother and son both try to find a love match."},{"s":3,"e":3,"t":"Series 3, Show 3","a":"1987-09-19","l":60,"d":"Self-confessed attention seeker Plum chooses between an insurance broker James, a security officer and a plumber. Jose is hoping to waltz into the sunset with his pick of three theatrical girls. Last week's contestants return to reveal how their dates went."},{"s":3,"e":4,"t":"Series 3, Show 4","a":"1987-09-26","l":60,"d":"Fashion student Mia has the pick of blogger Howie, Geordie Declan and musician Elijah. Then Stephen from Blackpool chooses his date from bodybuilder Terri, teacher Julia and Marilyn Monroe impersonator Suzie."},{"s":3,"e":5,"t":"Series 3, Show 5","a":"1987-10-03","l":60,"d":"Criminologist Luke is about to be surprised by three gorgeous drag queens who are eagerly waiting on the other side of the wall. Also glamorous Glaswegian beautician Lauren has to choose between two best friends, Jamie and Steve, from Doncaster and recruitment consultant Max from London."},{"s":3,"e":6,"t":"Series 3, Show 6","a":"1987-10-10","l":60,"d":"Devorshka is back to pick another date, and she hopes that it will be more successful than her last one. Also hoping to be picked for a blind date are Katie from Gloucester, Welsh nurse Sarah and Bath beautician Lucie."},{"s":3,"e":7,"t":"Series 3, Show 7","a":"1987-10-17","l":60,"d":"Personal trainer Calvin and local hero Mark from Blackpool take their pick from three singletons each. Plus, Devorshka and Wes return from Morocco, and Larry and Sarah recount their pottery-based exploits."},{"s":3,"e":8,"t":"Series 3, Show 8","a":"1987-10-24","l":60,"d":"Looking for love this week are a bearded dragon, a guinea pig and a Staffie - and their owners Bex, Dawn and Chrystal, who are all hoping to be picked by pirate-fighting Jordan and his dog Lola. Last in the series."},{"s":3,"e":9,"t":"Series 3, Show 9","a":"1987-10-31","l":60,"d":"Paul O'Grady helps more singles look for love, starting with a wedding singer, who has to choose between three unseen strangers who have played a supporting role in many other women's big days, as a make-up artist, a weight-loss coach and a serial bridesmaid. The second contestant has a Blind Date history, having previously appeared on the original ITV show 26 years ago."},{"s":3,"e":10,"t":"Series 3, Show 10","a":"1987-11-07","l":60,"d":"Paul O'Grady hosts a revival of the dating show in which contestants must choose between three unseen suitors based on their answers to a series of questions. Taking part tonight are Laura from south Wales, who chooses between a Justin Timberlake impersonator, a sales advisor and an entrepreneur. Author Jean-Paul then decides between a psychic, a kickboxer and a dance-loving granny"},{"s":3,"e":11,"t":"Series 3, Show 11","a":"1987-11-14","l":60},{"s":3,"e":12,"t":"Series 3, Show 12","a":"1987-11-21","l":60},{"s":3,"e":13,"t":"Series 3, Show 13","a":"1987-11-28","l":60},{"s":3,"e":14,"t":"Series 3, Show 14","a":"1987-12-05","l":60},{"s":3,"e":15,"t":"Series 3, Show 15","a":"1987-12-12","l":60},{"s":3,"e":16,"t":"Series 3, Show 16","a":"1987-12-19","l":60},{"s":3,"e":17,"t":"Series 3, Show 17","a":"1987-12-25","l":60},{"s":4,"e":1,"t":"Series 4, Show 1","a":"1988-09-03","l":60,"d":"Paul O'Grady helps more singles look for love, starting with a wedding singer, who has to choose between three unseen strangers who have played a supporting role in many other women's big days, as a make-up artist, a weight-loss coach and a serial bridesmaid. The second contestant has a Blind Date history, having previously appeared on the original ITV show 26 years ago."},{"s":4,"e":2,"t":"Series 4, Show 2","a":"1988-09-10","l":60,"d":"Laura chooses between a sales advisor, an entrepreneur and an impersonator. Jean-Paul picks from a psychic, a kickboxer and a super-glam granny. Plus last week's winners return to tell the tale."},{"s":4,"e":3,"t":"Series 4, Show 3","a":"1988-09-17","l":60,"d":"Retired dance school owner Ken is hoping to find his Barbie, while cheeky Essex estate agent Brandon is also looking to make a match. Plus, last week's winners return to tell the tale."},{"s":4,"e":4,"t":"Series 4, Show 4","a":"1988-09-24","l":60,"d":"Sales executive Jack is looking for his Mr Right, while Lewis is hoping to find a match from among three lovable ladies. Plus, last week's winners return to tell the tale."},{"s":4,"e":5,"t":"Series 4, Show 5","a":"1988-10-01","l":60,"d":"Laura from Barnsley has high hopes for a tradesman, and Derby-dweller Tom takes his pick from three bachelorettes. Plus, last week's winners return to share their tales."},{"s":4,"e":6,"t":"Series 4, Show 6","a":"1988-10-08","l":60,"d":"Spanish teacher Carlos is looking to finally meet 'the one' after years of travelling. Matt from Sandhurst takes his pick from three singles. Plus, last week's winners return to share their tales."},{"s":4,"e":7,"t":"Series 4, Show 7","a":"1988-10-15","l":60,"d":"Welsh bodybuilder Aaron picks between three models. Beauty consultant Jordan's line-up makes for a Blind Date first."},{"s":4,"e":8,"t":"Series 4, Show 8","a":"1988-10-22","l":60,"d":"Single dad George picks between three single mums who have all brought their daughters to the show. Mia chooses from the entertaining trio of a panto performer, a voice artist and a magician. Plus the results of last week's blind dates. Last in the series."},{"s":4,"e":9,"t":"Series 4, Show 9","a":"1988-10-29","l":60,"d":"Legal archivist Vanessa appraises a Hugh Grant lookalike, a wrestler and a barber, while a car salesman joins two twins in trying to impress estate agent Charlotte. Plus, the results of last week's blind dates."},{"s":4,"e":10,"t":"Series 4, Show 10","a":"1988-11-05","l":60,"d":"Paul O'Grady hosts a revival of the dating show in which a Swedish flight attendant and an animal lover who seeks the advice of his chihuahua choose between three unseen suitors. Plus, a chance to catch up on the previous episode's couples, and discover how their trips to Rome and Barbados turned out."},{"s":4,"e":11,"t":"Series 4, Show 11","a":"1988-11-12","l":60,"d":"Paul O'Grady hosts the revival of the dating show, in which an actress and entertainer, and a 79-year-old man must choose between three unseen suitors based on their answers to a series of questions. Plus, the couples from the previous episode return to the studio to reveal how they got on with their farming and bungee-jumping themed dates."},{"s":4,"e":12,"t":"Series 4, Show 12","a":"1988-11-19","l":60,"d":"Paul O'Grady hosts the dating show, with a lettings agent choosing between a hairstylist, an actor and a fitness instructor, while a charity shop manager poses questions to a fashion writer, a hotel receptionist and a club promotions manager. Plus, a chance 